  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is defined for <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />If <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then the above expression is positive.<br />If <math><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the above inequality still holds.<br />If <math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>as</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Hence, the domain of <math><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>",
